<p id="mwBQ"><b id="mwBg">Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Barmak</b> was one of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Barmakids" title="Barmakids" id="mwBw">Barmakids</a>, a family of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Iranian_peoples" title="Iranian peoples" id="mwCA">Iranian</a> functionaries who rose to great power under the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Abbasid" title="Abbasid" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCQ">Abbasid</a> caliph <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Harun_al-Rashid" title="Harun al-Rashid" id="mwCg">Harun al-Rashid</a> (<span style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt7" typeof="mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"reign","href":"./Template:Reign"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"786"},"2":{"wt":"809"}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwCw"><abbr title="reigned" about="#mwt8" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" data-mw='{"attribs":[[{"txt":"title"},{"html":"&lt;span typeof=\"mw:Nowiki\" id=\"mwDA\">reigned&lt;/span>"}]]}'>r.</abbr><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>786–809</span>).</p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}' id="mwDQ"/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwDg"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Life">Life</h2>
<p id="mwDw">He was the brother of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Yahya_ibn_Khalid" title="Yahya ibn Khalid" id="mwEA">Yahya ibn Khalid</a>,<sup about="#mwt9" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601036_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601036"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601036-1"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Barthold"},"2":{"wt":"Sourdel"},"3":{"wt":"1960"},"p":{"wt":"1036"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Muhammad_ibn_Khalid_ibn_Barmak#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601036-1" id="mwEQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEw">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFA">]</span></span></a></sup> whose appointment as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Vizier_(Abbasid_Caliphate)" title="Vizier (Abbasid Caliphate)" id="mwFQ">vizier</a> by Caliph <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Harun_al-Rashid" title="Harun al-Rashid" id="mwFg">Harun al-Rashid</a> in 786 began the family's twenty-year domination of the Abbasid Caliphate's public affairs.<sup about="#mwt12" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601034_2-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601034"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601034-2"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Barthold"},"2":{"wt":"Sourdel"},"3":{"wt":"1960"},"p":{"wt":"1034"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Muhammad_ibn_Khalid_ibn_Barmak#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601034-2" id="mwFw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGQ">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGg">]</span></span></a></sup> Muhammad served as the Caliph's chamberlain (<span title="Arabic-language romanization" about="#mwt15" typeof="mw:Transclusion" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Transliteration","href":"./Template:Transliteration"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"ar"},"2":{"wt":"[[hajib]]"}},"i":0}}]}' id="mwGw"><i lang="ar-Latn"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Hajib" title="Hajib">hajib</a></i></span>) from 788 to 795.<sup about="#mwt16" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601036_1-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601036"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601036-1"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Barthold"},"2":{"wt":"Sourdel"},"3":{"wt":"1960"},"p":{"wt":"1036"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Muhammad_ibn_Khalid_ibn_Barmak#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601036-1" id="mwHA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHw">]</span></span></a></sup> He was replaced by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Al-Fadl_ibn_al-Rabi" title="Al-Fadl ibn al-Rabi" id="mwIA">al-Fadl ibn al-Rabi</a>,<sup about="#mwt19" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBosworth1989152–153_3-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBosworth1989152–153"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBosworth1989152–153-3"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Bosworth"},"2":{"wt":"1989"},"pp":{"wt":"152–153"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Muhammad_ibn_Khalid_ibn_Barmak#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBosworth1989152–153-3" id="mwIQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwIg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIw">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJA">]</span></span></a></sup> who in the anecdotes of the time appears both as the Barmakids' foil and main antagonist at court.<sup about="#mwt22" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKennedy200633,_79_4-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEKennedy200633, 79"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKennedy200633,_79-4"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Kennedy"},"2":{"wt":"2006"},"pp":{"wt":"33, 79"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Muhammad_ibn_Khalid_ibn_Barmak#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKennedy200633,_79-4" id="mwJQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJw">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwKQ">Muhammad also served Harun al-Rashid as governor in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Yemen" title="Yemen" id="mwKg">Yemen</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Jazira_(caliphal_province)" title="Jazira (caliphal province)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKw">Jazira</a>.<sup about="#mwt25" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTECrone1980176_5-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTECrone1980176"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECrone1980176-5"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Crone"},"2":{"wt":"1980"},"p":{"wt":"176"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Muhammad_ibn_Khalid_ibn_Barmak#cite_note-FOOTNOTECrone1980176-5" id="mwLA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLg">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwMA">He was the only Barmakid to be spared during the family's abrupt fall in 803,<sup about="#mwt28" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601036_1-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601036"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601036-1"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Barthold"},"2":{"wt":"Sourdel"},"3":{"wt":"1960"},"p":{"wt":"1036"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Muhammad_ibn_Khalid_ibn_Barmak#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBartholdSourdel19601036-1" id="mwMQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMw">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt31" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEvan_Bladel2012_6-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEvan Bladel2012"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEvan_Bladel2012-6"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"van Bladel"},"2":{"wt":"2012"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Muhammad_ibn_Khalid_ibn_Barmak#cite_note-FOOTNOTEvan_Bladel2012-6" id="mwNQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNw">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt34" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBosworth1989219,_222,_224_7-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBosworth1989219, 222, 224"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBosworth1989219,_222,_224-7"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Bosworth"},"2":{"wt":"1989"},"pp":{"wt":"219, 222, 224"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Muhammad_ibn_Khalid_ibn_Barmak#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBosworth1989219,_222,_224-7" id="mwOQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwOg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOw">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPA">]</span></span></a></sup> likely because he had reported on the attempted flight of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Alid" title="Alid" class="mw-redirect" id="mwPQ">Alid</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Yahya_ibn_Abdallah" title="Yahya ibn Abdallah" id="mwPg">Yahya ibn Abdallah</a>, who had been released by Yahya's son <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Ja'far_ibn_Yahya" title="Ja'far ibn Yahya" id="mwPw">Ja'far</a>, contrary to the Caliph's orders to have him killed.<sup about="#mwt37" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMadelung2002243_8-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEMadelung2002243"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMadelung2002243-8"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Madelung"},"2":{"wt":"2002"},"p":{"wt":"243"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="./Muhammad_ibn_Khalid_ibn_Barmak#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMadelung2002243-8" id="mwQA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwQQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQg">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

